  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 AM MDT Thu May 14 2026\n\nWe are looking at a typical Spring time weather pattern over the\nnext seven days; things are looking dry with breezy or windy (but\nnot too windy) conditions each afternoon. For this afternoon and\nFriday, we will have a slow moving short wave trough moving \nacross central New Mexico. This system has very little moisture to\nwork with, so breezy southwest winds will be the main impact for \nthis afternoon and Friday afternoon. High temperatures today and \nFriday will run around 5 degrees above average. \n\nFor Saturday, a slow moving long wave trough will begin to move\ninto the southwest U.S. This system will keep our winds on\nSaturday in the breezy category (15 to 25 mph) and in the windy\ncategory (20 to 30 mph) for Sunday and Monday. We will see a few\ndegrees of cooling each day this weekend, with high temperatures\non Monday either near average or a few degrees below average. For\nTuesday and Wednesday of next week we will see a breezy zonal\n(west to east) flow set up across the region, which will keep us \ndry with high temperatures staying near seasonal averages.",
